   "variant_id": null,
   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "A tank holds \\( V(t) \\) liters of water shared equally among \\( N(t) \\) animals, where \\( t \\) is measured in days. At \\( t = 5 \\), \\( V(5) = 40 \\), \\( V'(5) = 18 \\), \\( N(5) = 7 \\), and \\( N'(5) = -1 \\). The water per animal is \\( W(t) = \\frac{V(t)}{N(t)} \\) liters. Find the value of \\( W'(5) \\), in liters per animal per day."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Rational",
         166,
         49
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Record the values at \\( t = 5 \\): \\( V(5) = 40 \\), \\( V'(5) = 18 \\), \\( N(5) = 7 \\), \\( N'(5) = -1 \\).",
         "mathjson": 18
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "By the quotient rule, \\( \\left(\\frac{V}{N}\\right)'(5) = \\frac{V'(5)N(5) - V(5)N'(5)}{[N(5)]^{2}} \\).",
         "mathjson": 40
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Substitute: \\( \\frac{(18)(7) - (40)(-1)}{(7)^{2}} = \\frac{166}{49} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            166,
            49
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "So \\( W'(5) = \\frac{166}{49} \\) liters per animal per day at \\( t = 5 \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            166,
            49
         ]
      }
   ],
